sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Customer as Customer / User
    participant Gateway as Nginx Gateway (:80)
    participant AS as auth-service (8081)
    participant AuthDB as auth_db (User / ResetToken)
    participant Mailpit as Mailpit Mock SMTP (:1025)
    participant Audit as AuditService (M8)

    Customer->>Gateway: POST /api/v1/auth/password/forgot { email }
    Gateway->>AS: Forward request
    AS->>AuthDB: Query user by email
    alt User found
        AS->>AS: Generate secure random token (UUID / cryptographically strong)
        AS->>AS: Compute SHA-256 hash of token
        AS->>AuthDB: INSERT INTO password_reset_tokens (hashed_token, expires_at: +30m, used: false)
        AS->>Mailpit: Dispatch reset email containing raw token link
        AS->>Audit: Log PASSWORD_RESET_REQUESTED (no sensitive details)
    else User not found
        AS->>AS: No-op / constant-time delay simulation
    end
    AS-->>Customer: 202 Accepted { "message": "If account exists, instructions were sent" }

    Note over Customer,Mailpit: Customer receives email at Mailpit and clicks reset link

    Customer->>Gateway: POST /api/v1/auth/password/reset { token, newPassword }
    Gateway->>AS: Forward request
    AS->>AS: Compute SHA-256 hash of provided token
    AS->>AuthDB: Query password_reset_tokens WHERE hashed_token AND used = false AND expires_at > NOW()
    alt Token valid and unexpired
        AS->>AS: Hash new password using BCrypt (rounds: 12)
        AS->>AuthDB: UPDATE users SET password_hash = :newHash
        AS->>AuthDB: UPDATE password_reset_tokens SET used = true
        AS->>AuthDB: Invalidate / delete all active refresh tokens for user
        AS->>Audit: Log PASSWORD_RESET_SUCCESS
        AS-->>Customer: 200 OK { "message": "Password successfully reset" }
    else Invalid or Expired Token
        AS-->>Customer: 400 Bad Request { "code": "INVALID_TOKEN", "message": "Token expired or invalid" }
    end
